    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d544">

                <pb facs="0953" n="819" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg819"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source"> Truman Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 544<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Secretary of
                        War</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stimson</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d544-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">On
                                Board the</hi> U. S. S. “<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Augusta</hi>”</placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-12">12 July 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have received your No. 95<anchor n="2" xml:id="d544-f2"/> and discussed it with
                    the President. As the question is a complicated one, I suggest we talk it over
                    at <hi rendition="#small-caps">Terminal</hi>.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d544-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d544-f1-content">
                <p>It has not been determined whether this message was dispatched first and then
                    superseded by <ref target="#d545">document No. 545</ref>, or whether <ref
                        target="#d545">document No. 545</ref> was dispatched first and then
                    superseded by this message.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d544-f2" n="2" xml:id="d544-f2-content">
